      "seed": 1696784745,
      "version": 1209,
      "versionNonce": 216972967,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793811322565,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Functional Requirements : \n    1. Resolve domain queries via UDP/TCP Port.\n    2. Enforce TTL policies by caching and expiring records.\n    3. Perform active TCP/HTTP health checks on backend origin servers and route traffic only to healthy IPs.\n    4. Provide a REST API for tenant CRUD operations on DNS zones and records.\n    5. Support failover when an endpoint becomes unhealthy.\n\n2. Non - Functional Requirements : \n    1. Ultra low latency < 10ms and multi-tier caching.\n    2. A >> C (Consistency for DNS updates and health status change)\n    3. High Read to Write ratio e.g: 100,000 : 1\n    4. Durability: DNS records and health-check configuration must not be lost.\n\n3. Back of the envelope : \n    1. Traffic : 1M QPS globally.\n    2. Bandwidth : 1M QPS * 100B (avg DNS Response) = 100MB/s\n    3. Storage : 100M active records * 1Kb = 100 GB (LRU Cache)\n\n4. API Design : \n    1. List DNS Records : GET : /v1/api/zones/{zone}/records\n    2. Create/Update record : POSt : /v1/api/zones/{zone}/records\n    3. Configure health check : POST : v1/api/health-checks\n    4. Get endpoint health : GET : /v1/api/health-checks/{id}\n\n5. Data Models and Entities : \n    1. DNSRecord : recordID, domain, recordType, values, ttl, policy\n    2. Health check : checkID, endpoint, protocol, interval, timeout, threshold\n    3. Health status : endpoint, status, lastCheckAt\n\n6. HLD : ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Functional Requirements : \n    1. Resolve domain queries via UDP/TCP Port.\n    2. Enforce TTL policies by caching and expiring records.\n    3. Perform active TCP/HTTP health checks on backend origin servers and route traffic only to healthy IPs.\n    4. Provide a REST API for tenant CRUD operations on DNS zones and records.\n    5. Support failover when an endpoint becomes unhealthy.\n\n2. Non - Functional Requirements : \n    1. Ultra low latency < 10ms and multi-tier caching.\n    2. A >> C (Consistency for DNS updates and health status change)\n    3. High Read to Write ratio e.g: 100,000 : 1\n    4. Durability: DNS records and health-check configuration must not be lost.\n\n3. Back of the envelope : \n    1. Traffic : 1M QPS globally.\n    2. Bandwidth : 1M QPS * 100B (avg DNS Response) = 100MB/s\n    3. Storage : 100M active records * 1Kb = 100 GB (LRU Cache)\n\n4. API Design : \n    1. List DNS Records : GET : /v1/api/zones/{zone}/records\n    2. Create/Update record : POSt : /v1/api/zones/{zone}/records\n    3. Configure health check : POST : v1/api/health-checks\n    4. Get endpoint health : GET : /v1/api/health-checks/{id}\n\n5. Data Models and Entities : \n    1. DNSRecord : recordID, domain, recordType, values, ttl, policy\n    2. Health check : checkID, endpoint, protocol, interval, timeout, threshold\n    3. Health status : endpoint, status, lastCheckAt\n\n6. HLD : ",
