      "index": "ap",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1849776983,
      "version": 168,
      "versionNonce": 1352837847,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793892358959,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "7. Bottlenecks and Failures : \n    1. Health Check Storms: If every edge resolver independently pings origin servers, a CDN with 10,000 nodes\nwill accidentally DDoS the origin. Fix: Decouple health checking into a centralized worker cluster that pings\norigins once, publishing state changes via Kafka to the edge nodes.\n\n    2. Stale-While-Revalidate: If a critical domain's TTL expires and Cassandra is temporarily slow, the resolver\nmust serve the stale L2 cache data while asynchronously fetching the new record in the background to ensure\nstrict 10ms SLA compliance.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "7. Bottlenecks and Failures : \n    1. Health Check Storms: If every edge resolver independently pings origin servers, a CDN with 10,000 nodes will accidentally DDoS the origin. Fix: Decouple health checking into a centralized worker cluster that pings origins once, publishing state changes via Kafka to the edge nodes.\n\n    2. Stale-While-Revalidate: If a critical domain's TTL expires and Cassandra is temporarily slow, the resolver must serve the stale L2 cache data while asynchronously fetching the new record in the background to ensure strict 10ms SLA compliance.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
